708	RISK-1241	A0981_Gipiškis2024	Encouraging downstream provider to evaluate models for deployment-specific failure modes	Testing & Auditing	In some cases, AI system deployers are better positioned to perform certain risk management measures on the AI model in a provided AI system, relative to upstream model providers. For example, they understand their use case better and are more easily able to predict foreseeable misuse or failure modes. These evaluations can inform upstream model providers, or inform supplementary mitigations by the deployer.
