9957	RISK-302	A0831_UK Government2023	Recurrent Performance analysis of AI models	Post-deployment Monitoring	Measure the performance of AI models and systems on an ongoing basis. A decline in model performance could be an indication of an attack or could indicate that a model is encountering data that is different from that which it was trained on. Either way, further investigation may be required.
9954	RISK-302	A0019_Bengio2025	Safety of The Intended Function	Model Safety Engineering	An approach that requires engineers to provide evidence that a system is safe when operating as intended.This approach is used in many engineering fields, such as in the construction and testing of road vehicles.
9951	RISK-302	A0002_Bengio2025	Benchmarks	Testing & Auditing	A standardised, often quantitative test or metric used to evaluate and compare the performance of AI systems on a fixed set of tasks designed to represent real- world usage
13240	RISK-303	A0919_UK Government2023	Audits for Biases in the Data	Data Governance	Training data that is imbalanced or inaccurate can result in an AI system being less accurate for people with certain personal characteristics or providing a skewed picture of particular groups. Ensuring a better balance in the training data could help to address this.
