1407	RISK-397	A0953_Gipiškis2024	Evaluations for truthful outputs	Testing & Auditing	AI systems can be evaluated for truthfulness when answering questions, includ- ing in contexts where humans tend to give incorrect but widely-accepted answers (i.e., popular misconceptions). Evaluations detect incorrect facts learned about the world, inadequate capabilities of the AI system, and misleading outputs by the AI system [121].
1408	RISK-397	A1001_Gipiškis2024	Informative and powerful benchmarks	Testing & Auditing	Developers of GPAI systems can select benchmarks that are difficult enough to be informative about the capabilities of their AI systems, and cover a large spec- trum of domains in order to signal areas where the GPAI system is performing poorly [120].Suitable benchmarks contain no label errors, are not vulnerable to being bench- mark contaminants, and are often audited by independent domain experts if they contain domain-specific questions. For multimodal GPAI systems, good benchmarks cover every modality, especially the interaction of different modalities.
