1415	RISK-398	A0935_Gipiškis2024	Restrict web access during AI training	Model Safety Engineering	Developers can restrict or disable AI systems’ internet access during training. For example, developers can restrict web access to read-only (e.g., by disabling write-access through HTTP POST requests and access to web forms) or limit the access of the AI system to a local network
1416	RISK-398	A0987_Gipiškis2024	Sandboxing of AI Systems	Testing & Auditing	AI systems can be developed and tested within a sandbox, (a secure and iso- lated environment used for separating running programs), such that outside access to information within the sandbox is restricted. Within this environ- ment, resources such as storage and memory space, and network access, would be disallowed or heavily restricted [15]. With sandboxing, dangerous or harmful outputs generated during testing will be contained.
