1619	RISK-523	A0987_Gipiškis2024	Sandboxing of AI Systems	Testing & Auditing	AI systems can be developed and tested within a sandbox, (a secure and iso- lated environment used for separating running programs), such that outside access to information within the sandbox is restricted. Within this environ- ment, resources such as storage and memory space, and network access, would be disallowed or heavily restricted [15]. With sandboxing, dangerous or harmful outputs generated during testing will be contained.
1620	RISK-523	A0019_Bengio2025	Safety of The Intended Function	Model Safety Engineering	An approach that requires engineers to provide evidence that a system is safe when operating as intended.This approach is used in many engineering fields, such as in the construction and testing of road vehicles.
1621	RISK-523	A0945_Gipiškis2024	Audits with specific scoped goals	Testing & Auditing	Audits of AI systems will be easier to perform, and have clearer results if the scope and goals of the evaluation are formulated as precisely as possible [157], or have a connection to concrete existing policy.
