6696	RISK-566	A0955_Gipiškis2024	Benchmarks for Situational Awareness	Testing & Auditing	A model is situationally aware if it internally represents that it is a machine learning model and if it can accurately infer or act on model-relevant facts - e.g., if it is currently in training, testing, evaluation or deployment, or the desired outcome of an evaluation. Some benchmarks exist for situational awareness of AI models, which test whether the AI models can classify stereotypical inputs from training, test- ing, evaluation and deployment as such, and whether the AI model can use this information correctly to take actions in the world [25, 111].
