6020	RISK-729	A1001_Gipiškis2024	Informative and powerful benchmarks	Testing & Auditing	Developers of GPAI systems can select benchmarks that are difficult enough to be informative about the capabilities of their AI systems, and cover a large spec- trum of domains in order to signal areas where the GPAI system is performing poorly [120].Suitable benchmarks contain no label errors, are not vulnerable to being bench- mark contaminants, and are often audited by independent domain experts if they contain domain-specific questions. For multimodal GPAI systems, good benchmarks cover every modality, especially the interaction of different modalities.
6021	RISK-729	A0945_Gipiškis2024	Audits with specific scoped goals	Testing & Auditing	Audits of AI systems will be easier to perform, and have clearer results if the scope and goals of the evaluation are formulated as precisely as possible [157], or have a connection to concrete existing policy.
1973	RISK-740	A0019_Bengio2025	Safety of The Intended Function	Model Safety Engineering	An approach that requires engineers to provide evidence that a system is safe when operating as intended.This approach is used in many engineering fields, such as in the construction and testing of road vehicles.
6022	RISK-729	A0943_Gipiškis2024	Red teaming to test the resilience of open-weights models to fine-tuning	Testing & Auditing	Before the release of open-weights models, red teamers can test the resilience of safety training against fine-tuning. Safety training may be partially or fully overridden by fine-tuning intentionally (e.g., by malicious actors) or uninten- tionally (e.g., by fine tuning an AI model for a specific use case)
