5501	RISK-974	A0955_Gipiškis2024	Benchmarks for Situational Awareness	Testing & Auditing	A model is situationally aware if it internally represents that it is a machine learning model and if it can accurately infer or act on model-relevant facts - e.g., if it is currently in training, testing, evaluation or deployment, or the desired outcome of an evaluation. Some benchmarks exist for situational awareness of AI models, which test whether the AI models can classify stereotypical inputs from training, test- ing, evaluation and deployment as such, and whether the AI model can use this information correctly to take actions in the world [25, 111].
5502	RISK-974	A1001_Gipiškis2024	Informative and powerful benchmarks	Testing & Auditing	Developers of GPAI systems can select benchmarks that are difficult enough to be informative about the capabilities of their AI systems, and cover a large spec- trum of domains in order to signal areas where the GPAI system is performing poorly [120].Suitable benchmarks contain no label errors, are not vulnerable to being bench- mark contaminants, and are often audited by independent domain experts if they contain domain-specific questions. For multimodal GPAI systems, good benchmarks cover every modality, especially the interaction of different modalities.
