2448	RISK-976	A0907_UK Government2023	Monitoring and Safeguard Efficacy	Testing & Auditing	Regularly assess monitoring and safeguard efficacy and continually invest in improvements. Regular assessment of monitoring efficacy can build an understanding of the success rate and speed of issue detection, on which deployment decisions may be based. These assessments may draw, for instance, on the results of internal and external red-teaming efforts, random audits of usage logs, what may be ‘best practice’, as well as available information about real-world misuse. Risks are expected to increase as AI capabilities increase. Hence, active increases in investment in safety, security, and monitoring may be valuable.
