2580	RISK-1067	A0987_Gipiškis2024	Sandboxing of AI Systems	Testing & Auditing	AI systems can be developed and tested within a sandbox, (a secure and iso- lated environment used for separating running programs), such that outside access to information within the sandbox is restricted. Within this environ- ment, resources such as storage and memory space, and network access, would be disallowed or heavily restricted [15]. With sandboxing, dangerous or harmful outputs generated during testing will be contained.
2576	RISK-1067	A0945_Gipiškis2024	Audits with specific scoped goals	Testing & Auditing	Audits of AI systems will be easier to perform, and have clearer results if the scope and goals of the evaluation are formulated as precisely as possible [157], or have a connection to concrete existing policy.
