4062	RISK-192	A0946_Gipiškis2024	Evaluating explainability method sensitivity to data inputs and model parameters	Testing & Auditing	Model parameter and data randomization tests can be employed as sanity checks [2] to determine the relationship between a model, its inputs, and the explainability method. If an explanation is independent from or insensitive to the underlying model or the input data, it would indicate a lack of reliability of the explainability method.
4063	RISK-192	A0955_Gipiškis2024	Benchmarks for Situational Awareness	Testing & Auditing	A model is situationally aware if it internally represents that it is a machine learning model and if it can accurately infer or act on model-relevant facts - e.g., if it is currently in training, testing, evaluation or deployment, or the desired outcome of an evaluation. Some benchmarks exist for situational awareness of AI models, which test whether the AI models can classify stereotypical inputs from training, test- ing, evaluation and deployment as such, and whether the AI model can use this information correctly to take actions in the world [25, 111].
