1631	RISK-534	A0947_Gipiškis2024	Enforcing model output interpretability post-training	Model Safety Engineering	While a resulting trained model may be opaque with respect to its predictions, the final output in a system that involves the model can nonetheless be com- pletely interpretable.For example, a neuro-symbolic system for robot navigation can use a language model to generate potential navigation plans, then have a deterministic solver simulate executing valid plans [128]. The optimal plan found is executed in the real world and is interpretable.
