6717	RISK-575	A0787_UK Government2023	Model Evaluation of Controllability	Testing & Auditing	Evaluate models for controllability issues (i.e. propensities to apply their capabilities in ways that neither the models’ users nor the models’ developers want). This could include, for example, autonomous replication and adaptation (i.e. capabilities that could allow a model to copy and run itself on other computer systems).
